  "limitations": "Polynomial degree at most 20; no expression evaluation, arbitrary callback, discontinuity support, complex roots, root multiplicity estimate or promise to find every root. A same-sign bracket is rejected. Coefficient scaling and near-multiple roots can limit residual/forward accuracy; the termination test bounds bracket width rather than certifying an exact zero. A zero endpoint is accepted even if the bracket is reversed.",
  "port_notes": "Port of scipy/optimize/Zeros/brentq.c at the pinned commit. Preserves the sequential C swap (new xblk is old xcur), secant/inverse-quadratic acceptance rule and bisection safeguard. Horner polynomial evaluation replaces an arbitrary C callback. Zero-division during attempted interpolation falls back to bisection as C nonfinite arithmetic would. Endpoint iteration count is explicitly zero rather than exposing an uninitialized statistic. Original author credit: Written by Charles Harris; header modifications by Travis Oliphant. Contact-only first lines are not redistributed; legal license notices are intact.",
